  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 85,
      "char_start": 29,
      "char_end": 260,
      "text": "\"\n\nHe climbed up on Salve's back, and so on to the top of the wall; drew\nSalve up beside him, and then sprang down into the little garden and\nbegan to roll about on the grass as if he had taken leave of his senses,\ncrying, \"Salvado"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 86,
      "char_start": 809,
      "char_end": 1113,
      "text": "She threw her head back then with\na triumphant, scornful laugh that showed her dazzling white teeth; and\nSalve inferred that her brother must have killed some person or other in\nMonte Video, probably in self-preservation, and that he was afraid the\npolice here, in Rio, should have had information of it"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 88,
      "char_start": 1399,
      "char_end": 1724,
      "text": "She used to remain during the greater part of the\nday on the shady side of the house, or on the little veranda, with\nacachacas and water by her side, and incessantly smoking and rolling\ncigarettes; and she was often quite drunk as she mumbled her Ave Maria,\nand told her beads on her knees before going to bed in the evening"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 89,
      "char_start": 1309,
      "char_end": 1772,
      "text": "The second morning of his stay in the house Salve had perceived that\nthere was a want of money; and having heard the brother and sister\nquarrelling one day when both were in a bad humour, he thought it best\nto carry out, at the first convenient moment, the determination at which\nhe had arrived, and handed over to Federigo what money he had, with the\nexception of a single silver piastre, saying, \"That it was only right he\nshould pay for his lodging and board"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 90,
      "char_start": 634,
      "char_end": 874,
      "text": "Her range of ideas was apparently not extensive, as her\nquestions always turned upon the same topic--namely, what the women were\nlike in his country; so that he soon came to know by heart all the\nSpanish terms which related to that subject"
    }
  ],
